-- check/bad (core): a demand carried through a beni function's parameter
-- and across a module boundary (transparent-effects-proposal.md §15.3,
-- §15.4). `Plat` declares the primitive and the `sync` parameter; `Lib`'s
-- `onType` hands its parameter to it inside a lambda, so its summary says
-- the parameter is `sync` with nothing written; `Main` passes suspending
-- functions to `Lib.onType` and is refused there. The chain stops at the
-- first imported value (decision 7a): `Lib.load` suspends because `Lib`'s
-- record says so, and nothing of `Lib`'s body is named.
pub foreign suspends get : Int -> String


pub foreign pure onEvent : sync (Int -> String) -> Int
